Subject: [PATCH 10/16] Radar: reveal blips with the sweep and draw them as
 complete shapes

Mirror-node blips previously drew as always-on solid shapes (adhoc #135)
and were painted before the central latency text, whose backing disc
clipped their inner halves into crescents. Reworked the RelayRadarWidget
blip pass so it behaves like a real radar scope:

- Blips stay dark until the sweep's leading edge wipes across them, then
  flare to full brightness and fade out along a phosphor trail before the
  next revolution relights them.
- The pass now runs last, after the latency read-out, and sits on a wider
  ring (r*0.80) so every blip reads as a full circle (or an integrity
  triangle) instead of a slice clipped by the text disc or dish edge.

