Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 14:18:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] adhoc #144: memoize the catalog scan in
 _online_source_of_truth (info/refs hang)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Production logs (2026-07-18 14:08 EDT) show git-upload-pack info/refs
requests dying with the Pyodide "Cannot enter into task" RuntimeError,
followed by the Workers runtime canceling the request as hung — the same
event-loop-congestion failure fixed on 2026-07-12 (0f911e76) by memoizing
the decrypted public catalog.

_online_source_of_truth, added after that fix, reintroduced the pattern:
it runs on EVERY public clone request (info/refs and the upload-pack POST)
and, for a mirror namespace, re-scanned + sequentially decrypted the whole
public repo catalog per request. Under a clone burst that congests the
single Worker event loop until the runtime cancels in-flight requests.

Reuse the shared per-isolate _decrypted_public_catalog memo instead, so a
burst pays for one decrypt pass. Its active-node filter is harmless here:
a candidate source must pass _source_has_live_host anyway, and a node with
a connected host is active.

