From 1be249a3e9bebcd132b4917eadc0caa42603085c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forkmesh <forkmesh@users.forkmesh.local>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 14:18:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] Fix rebuild & restart blocked by invisible
 merged-but-Running sessions
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The restart gate (anyAgentRunning) counted a session whose stored status
was still Running even when the session was merged — but the whole UI
(table cell, footer dot, tooltip) shows a merged session as "merged",
never as running, so the user correctly saw no running actions while the
rebuild sat on "Waiting for running actions to finish" (adhoc #143).
Worse, initAgents() auto-resumed such sessions on every app start
(spawning a live CLI process for them), and markAgentSessionRunning()'s
already-Running early-return meant the merged flag was never cleared, so
each restart resurrected the invisible blocker.

- anyAgentRunning() now mirrors the display logic: a merged session never
  counts as running.
- initAgents() settles merged Running/Queued sessions as Success instead
  of re-queuing them — their branch already landed.
- When the rebuild does have to wait, the restart log now names exactly
  which sessions block it (runningAgentBlockers), ending the guessing
  game that ran through adhoc #91/#104/#111/#116/#134.
- While queued, a 2s poll re-checks the gate as a safety net for any
  completion path that misses its maybeStartQueuedRebuild() call.

